    "didYouKnow": "Amasi is so beloved that it nearly cost Nelson Mandela his freedom: hiding from the police in a white Johannesburg suburb, he left a bottle of milk on the windowsill to sour into amasi, and two men outside wondered aloud why that house was making it — he had to move on that very night. The rusks earn their keep too: twice-baked to drive out every drop of moisture, they wait patiently in the tin for months.",
