      "Roughly crumble the rusks into a bowl — big rough chunks, not crumbs. Fine crumbs turn to porridge the second the amasi lands; chunks give you soft outsides and a middle that still bites back.",
      "Pour the cold amasi over.",
      "Now the one-minute law: let it stand for about a minute, no more. That's the sweet spot — creamy edges, crunchy heart. Walk away for five and you've made pap.",
